// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (dynamic)
//
// valid(v) joins T and F to ? at the merge / at the loop head: a use of
// a binding that may have been moved is refuted (D-0087), as a read that
// may be uninitialized is.
// A reborrow through `*r` on one branch only: deriv(a, *r, shared)
// is ? after the merge (D-0071).
// Two paths the body cannot relate (D-0022) are related at the call by
// `f`'s access summary (D-0282): refuted before the run.
// Two computed elements: only the values relate them.

import std;
fn f(ref<i32, exclusive> a, ref<i32, shared> b) : i32
{
    *a = 1;
    *b
}
fn main()
{
    array<i32, 2> v = [0, 0];
    usize i = 1;
    usize j = i * 1;
    f(&mut v[i], &v[j]);
}
